// TYPL-303: `require`/`ensure` are expr-core attribute words. At declaration
// start in a `.typl` file they are a profile violation, distinct from the
// interaction words TYPL-304 reports.
//
// This lives in its own file because recovery from a profile violation
// resynchronizes at the next typl or ridl top-level keyword, and a reserved
// word of another profile is not one — so a second violation in the same file
// is absorbed into the first one's error node.

package diag.ridl

require currentSpeed >= 0
